  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Reinforcing the response of current partners and additional support to nutrition and cash based responses in the Democratic Republic of Congo following increased humanitarian needs and scale up of humanitarian response</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This activity Reinforcing the response of current partners and additional support to nutrition and cash based responses in the Democratic Republic of Congo following increased humanitarian needs and scale up of humanitarian response is a component of Democratic Republic of Congo- Humanitarian Innovation, Response and Reform programme (DRCHIRRP)  reported by FCDO with a funding type of 109 - Multilateral organisation and a budget of &#xA3;30,000,000. It works in the following sector(s): Material relief assistance and services, Relief co-ordination and support services, Immediate post-emergency reconstruction and rehabilitation, Disaster prevention and preparedness.</narrative>
  </description>
